{"id": "EUVD-2026-88361", "enisaUuid": "eef89d6c-d71f-39ac-9e6b-e73110a7c44c", "description": "A flaw was found in kube-compare. When processing a 'container://' reference path, the tool incorrectly executes an untrusted container image's entrypoint instead of merely extracting data from a stopped container. This allows a remote attacker to achieve arbitrary code execution on the operator's workstation. If the Docker daemon requires elevated privileges, the untrusted code may execute with root-mediated daemon privileges, posing a significant security risk.", "datePublished": "2026-09-28T16:49:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-07T14:09:47", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74381", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74384", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74430", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:74435", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-87114", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2522945"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c73r-9gcf-qjwr", "CVE-2026-87114"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7e8c257f-7288-3b3e-8962-59523a3aa853", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4.21", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1790707362"}, {"id": "8720517a-bd03-37ec-946b-87aca095c132", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4.22", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1790718431"}, {"id": "a039508c-ca34-355a-812e-224bb00ae882", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4.19", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1790632105"}, {"id": "c2ec21d1-618a-32ce-8d9b-851cf0c2d35a", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform 4.20", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1790707563"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cb10533b-31d7-3039-b3ea-6382a99cd7